WEBVTT

00:00:02.017 --> 00:00:05.817
Hajimari no kaze yo

00:00:06.255 --> 00:00:10.089
Todoke Message

00:00:10.492 --> 00:00:19.423
'Itsudemo anato wo Shinjiteirukara'

00:00:20.202 --> 00:00:20.703
The Story of Saiunkoku

00:00:20.703 --> 00:00:28.744
The Story of Saiunkoku
Ano toki yume ni miteita
Sekai ni tatteirunoni

00:00:28.744 --> 00:00:29.073
The Story of Saiunkoku

00:00:29.278 --> 00:00:36.480
Miwatasu keshiki ni
Ashi wo sukoshi sukumase

00:00:36.852 --> 00:00:40.982
Dakedo ushiro furimukanaide

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:45.083
Aruiteyuki koto
Kimeta kara

00:00:45.394 --> 00:00:49.490
Miageta sora
Nana iro no niji

00:00:49.665 --> 00:00:53.066
Anata mo mitemasuka?

00:00:53.402 --> 00:00:57.395
Hajimari no kaze yo

00:00:57.706 --> 00:01:01.472
Todoke Message

00:01:01.877 --> 00:01:10.046
Yumeni kakedashita senaka
Mimamoru kara

00:01:10.486 --> 00:01:14.422
Maiagaru kaze yo

00:01:14.823 --> 00:01:18.623
Hi no hikari matoi

00:01:19.094 --> 00:01:28.526
Jiyuu no tsubasa de
Tsuyoku tobitatou

00:01:45.087 --> 00:01:47.055
I'm finally here.

00:01:51.827 --> 00:01:54.955
A month has passed since
Shurei Hong left the Royal Harem.

00:01:55.664 --> 00:02:00.192
Saiunkoku's capital, Kiyo, has been
suffering under the scorching sun.

00:02:00.602 --> 00:02:02.627
It is the middle of summer.

00:02:03.472 --> 00:02:05.906
This is just way too hot.

00:02:09.912 --> 00:02:11.470
Hey! Pull yourself together!

00:02:12.815 --> 00:02:15.807
One after another,
people collapsed in the excessive heat.

00:02:16.285 --> 00:02:19.311
Until soon, the court
found itself short staffed.

00:02:20.055 --> 00:02:25.015
To Borrow a Cat's Paw

00:02:27.262 --> 00:02:29.730
Don't overwork yourself
in this heat, Seiran.

00:02:30.499 --> 00:02:34.196
I'm only a granary guard.
It's not a job where I'll work too hard.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:36.670
Then I guess you'll be fine, but...!

00:02:36.738 --> 00:02:40.765
There's no need to worry. I'll be okay.
Well then, I'll be going.

00:02:52.287 --> 00:02:55.256
It's that time of year again.

00:02:58.861 --> 00:03:02.194
As a result of this extreme heat,
many people have been incapacitated...

00:03:02.264 --> 00:03:04.562
...and this is affecting
our daily work.

00:03:04.633 --> 00:03:07.932
In particular, our Ministry of Finance,
which is short staffed to begin with...

00:03:08.003 --> 00:03:09.527
...is in a critical situation.

00:03:09.605 --> 00:03:11.470
It is just as you heard.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:14.202
In light of this crisis, I'd like you to
consider lending staff to assist...

00:03:14.276 --> 00:03:15.937
...the Ministry of Finance.

00:03:16.011 --> 00:03:17.308
Ministry of Finance?

00:03:17.379 --> 00:03:19.847
Sending our subordinates to
work under that weirdo?

00:03:20.249 --> 00:03:22.717
- What should we do?
- It's unreasonable.

00:03:23.785 --> 00:03:26.583
If the Ministry of Finance
can't function properly...

00:03:26.655 --> 00:03:29.180
...funds cannot be distributed
in a timely manner.

00:03:29.258 --> 00:03:31.192
I imagine that would be
a problem to you all.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.785
This is a request and
not an order from the king.

00:03:33.862 --> 00:03:37.059
But don't you think that we should
help one another in times of crisis?

00:03:37.132 --> 00:03:38.599
W-We understand.

00:03:39.368 --> 00:03:41.063
Thank you very much.

00:03:41.136 --> 00:03:42.967
Senior Secretary Kou
is also very grateful.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.505
Is he serious?

00:03:46.942 --> 00:03:49.069
Well then, moving on
to the next issue.

00:03:49.211 --> 00:03:52.476
It has been reported that an increasing
number of bandits from Sa Province...!

00:03:56.985 --> 00:03:59.317
- That concludes today's session.
- Actually...

00:03:59.388 --> 00:04:01.618
...there is one other thing
we wish to discuss.

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:03.624
It concerns the
national examinations.

00:04:03.692 --> 00:04:06.991
We wish to allow women
to take part in the next sitting.

00:04:12.401 --> 00:04:16.030
We want the national examination
system opened to women!

00:04:20.075 --> 00:04:25.980
Um, so... although I'm lonely,
I still sleep by myself.

00:04:26.114 --> 00:04:28.446
Anony... uh...!

00:04:28.517 --> 00:04:30.348
It's pronounced "anonymous".

00:04:30.819 --> 00:04:33.720
This says, "I miss
Shurei's erhu very much."

00:04:34.156 --> 00:04:37.853
This says, "I want to sleep beside you
and feel your warmth."

00:04:38.694 --> 00:04:40.628
What's that supposed to mean?

00:04:40.696 --> 00:04:43.028
Okay, okay.
You don't have to read them!

00:04:43.098 --> 00:04:45.828
Turn the sheets over, and use
the back to practice your writing!

00:04:46.101 --> 00:04:48.069
We have more than
enough paper!

00:04:48.136 --> 00:04:49.296
Okay!

00:04:50.272 --> 00:04:52.797
Of all the things
that ridiculous man does...

00:04:52.874 --> 00:04:55.308
...some of them actually
come in handy.

00:04:57.079 --> 00:04:59.206
This is a gift from Anonymous.

00:04:59.614 --> 00:05:01.514
He says you can use these
to withstand the heat.

00:05:01.583 --> 00:05:03.847
No matter how you look at it,
these are too big.

00:05:04.252 --> 00:05:06.379
This is a gift from Anonymous.

00:05:07.189 --> 00:05:09.419
"I found these unusual
flowers in bloom."

00:05:10.058 --> 00:05:13.858
Manjushage.
Also known as the spider lily.

00:05:14.296 --> 00:05:16.230
Come on,
my home isn't a cemetery.

00:05:17.032 --> 00:05:19.125
A gift from Anonymous.

00:05:20.268 --> 00:05:22.236
Why boiled eggs?

00:05:22.904 --> 00:05:24.872
A gift from...!

00:05:29.544 --> 00:05:32.445
Honestly, that ridiculous man.

00:05:38.086 --> 00:05:39.451
Ryuki?

00:05:43.959 --> 00:05:45.221
Shurei!

00:05:45.761 --> 00:05:47.092
I love you.

00:05:47.162 --> 00:05:48.686
What are you saying?!

00:05:49.865 --> 00:05:52.333
I'm gonna marry this man.

00:05:52.401 --> 00:05:54.096
Sorry about this, Ryuki.

00:05:54.169 --> 00:05:55.193
Brother?

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:58.262
Seiran is so much more
mature and reliable.

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.633
You'll give us your blessing,
won't you?

00:06:01.076 --> 00:06:02.543
Ah, well, wait...!

00:06:03.011 --> 00:06:04.979
Bye then, brother-in-law.

00:06:05.247 --> 00:06:07.943
Good luck in finding your own
happiness, my real younger brother.

00:06:08.016 --> 00:06:09.608
H-Hey, wait!

00:06:16.024 --> 00:06:17.252
Get out.

00:06:17.492 --> 00:06:18.891
I'm sorry.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:22.396
It was such a delightful dream.
I couldn't help it.

00:06:22.664 --> 00:06:23.790
It was a nightmare.

00:06:27.969 --> 00:06:30.733
But that dream did have
some truth to it, didn't it?

00:06:30.806 --> 00:06:32.967
No! It was a nightmare!
A nightmare!

00:06:33.041 --> 00:06:36.408
Lady Shurei certainly is
about the right age for marriage.

00:06:36.478 --> 00:06:38.139
Regardless of whether
it's Seiran or not...

00:06:38.213 --> 00:06:40.010
...it would not be
out of the ordinary...

00:06:40.082 --> 00:06:42.175
...for her to receive a marriage
proposal from someone.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:45.947
But I always send her letters,
not to mention a lot of gifts!

00:06:48.423 --> 00:06:51.290
If I may ask, what was
the last gift you sent her?

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:53.325
A voodoo doll.

00:06:54.463 --> 00:06:55.987
The meaning behind that?

00:06:56.064 --> 00:06:59.431
Advisor Sho told me it's
a love charm.

00:06:59.801 --> 00:07:03.338
I put my own hair inside and focused
hard on her before sending it.

00:07:03.338 --> 00:07:06.034
That way the heat of my passion
will be delivered.

00:07:06.641 --> 00:07:09.667
B-But you haven't received
a single response from her, right?

00:07:10.879 --> 00:07:13.313
Maybe I shouldn't
have sent them anonymously.

00:07:14.082 --> 00:07:17.279
She probably doesn't know
who those gifts were from.

00:07:17.652 --> 00:07:19.677
That's it!
That has to be it!

00:07:21.323 --> 00:07:24.019
It's a long and difficult road, isn't it?

00:07:24.192 --> 00:07:25.159
Yeah.

00:07:25.227 --> 00:07:27.457
That's why I'm trying to think of
other ways to go about it.

00:07:28.029 --> 00:07:29.462
Koyu. What do you think?

00:07:29.664 --> 00:07:31.461
It needs to be rewritten.

00:07:33.602 --> 00:07:37.902
Something like this will never
win Secretary Kou's approval.

00:07:39.708 --> 00:07:42.506
After your sudden idiotic outburst
in the Imperial Court...

00:07:43.078 --> 00:07:45.740
...he left without saying a word,
didn't he?

00:07:46.515 --> 00:07:49.177
I guess I became impatient, so I...!

00:07:49.518 --> 00:07:53.818
It's next to impossible to get a proposal
passed once it's been rejected.

00:07:54.156 --> 00:07:56.647
Not to mention this proposal
is one that needs to be handled...

00:07:56.725 --> 00:07:58.852
...with a great deal of caution
in the first place.

00:07:58.927 --> 00:08:00.895
I understand that.
I'll rewrite it.

00:08:02.464 --> 00:08:03.488
Koyu.

00:08:03.865 --> 00:08:04.729
Yes?

00:08:04.799 --> 00:08:07.927
No matter what, this proposal
must be passed within the year.

00:08:11.373 --> 00:08:13.773
I hope summer will
pass by quickly.

00:08:25.086 --> 00:08:26.519
I just got back.

00:08:28.056 --> 00:08:29.182
Welcome back.

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:33.288
I'm home...!

00:08:34.629 --> 00:08:36.597
Oh, Seiran, welcome home.

00:08:37.098 --> 00:08:38.895
Who is that person?

00:08:38.967 --> 00:08:40.195
Um, he's...!

00:08:42.837 --> 00:08:45.499
Hey! Aren't you the Little Whirlwind?

00:08:50.545 --> 00:08:51.876
Seiran?

00:08:56.318 --> 00:08:58.343
Don't tell me it's you, Ensei!

00:08:58.420 --> 00:09:02.686
Correct. So it really is you.
Ah, long time no see.

00:09:03.792 --> 00:09:05.657
What are you doing here?

00:09:05.727 --> 00:09:09.424
It's a coincidence. A coincidence. I have
a bit of business to take care of in Kiyo.

00:09:09.497 --> 00:09:11.624
But I haven't really been
eating well lately.

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:15.227
Princess picked me up
after I collapsed.

00:09:15.804 --> 00:09:17.906
Now you can turn right around
and leave.

00:09:17.906 --> 00:09:20.170
What?! That's so cold!

00:09:20.909 --> 00:09:22.843
You can collapse in front of
someone else's door.

00:09:22.911 --> 00:09:25.038
If you'd like, I'll write you
a letter of introduction.

00:09:25.113 --> 00:09:26.774
You're so cruel.

00:09:27.983 --> 00:09:30.451
Seiran. What's all this
all of a sudden?

00:09:30.685 --> 00:09:34.018
Shurei, you can't pick up
things like this.

00:09:34.089 --> 00:09:36.148
Even if it was
lying on the ground.

00:09:36.224 --> 00:09:39.955
But he said he was on
the brink of death from starvation.

00:09:41.329 --> 00:09:44.127
He won't die. I guarantee it.

00:09:44.199 --> 00:09:47.032
So let's throw "it" out right now.
Right this instant!

00:09:47.902 --> 00:09:49.733
Don't you know one another?

00:09:49.804 --> 00:09:50.964
No we don't.

00:09:51.039 --> 00:09:54.770
Yeah, we do. We were just
reminiscing about old times, right?

00:09:54.843 --> 00:09:59.075
We're good buddies from way back,
aren't we? Uh... Seiran?

00:10:01.616 --> 00:10:04.710
So you're a friend of Seiran's.

00:10:05.587 --> 00:10:07.214
Well then, please make
yourself at home.

00:10:07.289 --> 00:10:09.280
Father should be home shortly.

00:10:13.295 --> 00:10:15.923
It seems you've been taken in
by a nice family.

00:10:15.997 --> 00:10:18.295
You look pretty happy,
which is great.

00:10:19.701 --> 00:10:23.797
I can't pay for food, but why don't I just
share stories from your past instead?

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:28.370
If you dare mention one word
about my past...

00:10:28.443 --> 00:10:30.434
...I'll cut off that head of yours!

00:10:34.716 --> 00:10:37.708
I was just kidding.
Ow, ow!

00:10:38.053 --> 00:10:43.013
The Story of Saiunkoku

00:10:44.626 --> 00:10:48.687
Ensei, is it?
What brings you here to Kiyo?

00:10:49.097 --> 00:10:51.258
Well, I've come here
to see someone.

00:10:51.333 --> 00:10:53.733
But it's a little difficult getting
to see them...

00:10:53.802 --> 00:10:55.929
...so I imagine
I'll be staying for a while.

00:10:56.004 --> 00:10:57.972
Is this a person of high rank?

00:10:58.039 --> 00:11:00.132
Y-Yes. You could say that.

00:11:00.275 --> 00:11:01.936
In that case,
can't you introduce him...

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:04.137
...to someone in the
Imperial Court, father?

00:11:04.679 --> 00:11:07.341
I'll ask for your help
if I've run out of all other options.

00:11:07.415 --> 00:11:09.883
It's secretive business
that brings me here, after all.

00:11:10.251 --> 00:11:13.084
Then you're welcome to stay here
until your business is taken care of.

00:11:13.755 --> 00:11:15.188
But sir...!

00:11:15.256 --> 00:11:17.349
He is your friend,
isn't he, Seiran?

00:11:17.759 --> 00:11:19.886
No, not exactly a friend.

00:11:20.895 --> 00:11:22.795
He's not a bad person, is he?

00:11:22.964 --> 00:11:24.625
That's true, but...!

00:11:24.699 --> 00:11:26.599
Then there's no problem,
is there?

00:11:26.668 --> 00:11:29.000
You should treat your friends
like they're important.

00:11:29.137 --> 00:11:30.001
Well...!

00:11:30.472 --> 00:11:32.804
If you don't mind the poor condition
of our house, that is.

00:11:32.874 --> 00:11:34.535
I've had enough of eating
and sleeping outside...

00:11:34.609 --> 00:11:36.577
...so this is more than
I could have wished for.

00:11:36.644 --> 00:11:39.738
Think nothing of it.
Just make yourself at home.

00:11:39.814 --> 00:11:42.840
Well then I'll happily accept your offer.
Seconds, please!

00:11:42.917 --> 00:11:44.043
You've had enough!

00:12:04.139 --> 00:12:05.231
Welcome back.

00:12:06.307 --> 00:12:08.537
I'll make some tea.
Have a seat.

00:12:09.144 --> 00:12:12.170
Um, I made steamed buns.

00:12:13.047 --> 00:12:14.344
Steamed buns?

00:12:15.550 --> 00:12:19.077
Lady Shurei taught me
when she was in the Royal Harem.

00:12:19.654 --> 00:12:23.146
Oh, then why don't we have them
as a snack with our tea?

00:12:24.859 --> 00:12:29.592
Thank you for going through the trouble
of taking Korin back to Sa Province.

00:12:30.298 --> 00:12:32.027
No, it was nothing.

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:45.038
Advisor Sa's wife,
who took Korin in, is...

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:49.109
...ah, how should I put it...
a surprising woman.

00:12:49.451 --> 00:12:53.285
She's an extraordinary person who
leaves a lasting impression, isn't she?

00:12:53.588 --> 00:12:54.589
Yes.

00:12:54.589 --> 00:12:59.617
If she's with a person like that, I'm
sure Korin will be able to recover. Or...

00:13:00.495 --> 00:13:03.123
...maybe that's just
my own wishful thinking.

00:13:03.698 --> 00:13:06.861
Korin will be all right. His wife
and Korin both loved Advisor Sa.

00:13:06.935 --> 00:13:09.733
She's the one person who loved
and was loved...

00:13:09.804 --> 00:13:11.533
...by Advisor Sa more than Korin.

00:13:11.606 --> 00:13:14.234
And just as important,
that woman is very strong.

00:13:14.309 --> 00:13:17.301
Staying with a person like her,
I'm sure everything will be all right.

00:13:17.946 --> 00:13:19.004
Yes.

00:13:19.614 --> 00:13:22.742
I hope it won't be too long
before Korin can smile again.

00:13:24.285 --> 00:13:25.809
Allow me to start.

00:13:26.421 --> 00:13:27.615
Your steamed buns.

00:13:27.689 --> 00:13:28.849
Ah, please do!

00:13:34.395 --> 00:13:37.660
Hey, it's delicious!
Just as good as Shurei's!

00:13:41.669 --> 00:13:46.333
Shoka, your tea's...
also... very tasty.

00:13:47.542 --> 00:13:52.275
No, it's not right! This would never
get the Finance Minister's approval.

00:13:57.452 --> 00:14:00.649
The Urin Army guarding the palace
is to be sent out to catch bandits?

00:14:01.589 --> 00:14:04.319
As you know, Shi's Provincial Army
has been so short-handed...

00:14:04.392 --> 00:14:06.519
...they would borrow a cat's paw.

00:14:06.594 --> 00:14:09.893
We don't have any hands
to spare, ourselves.

00:14:11.032 --> 00:14:13.762
Not to worry.
I will also lend a hand.

00:14:15.036 --> 00:14:18.005
This old man just wants a chance
to fight and go wild, doesn't he?

00:14:18.373 --> 00:14:19.806
While you're at it...

00:14:19.874 --> 00:14:21.933
...why don't you take
this opportunity...

00:14:22.010 --> 00:14:24.205
...to get that man
to return to the Urin Army?

00:14:24.612 --> 00:14:25.601
By "that man"...

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:28.080
...I'm assuming you're referring to
the granary guard, aren't you?

00:14:28.149 --> 00:14:31.983
Generals Koku and Haku
are also quite insistent.

00:14:45.533 --> 00:14:47.228
Where are you going?

00:14:47.302 --> 00:14:48.826
Where else would
I be going?

00:14:48.903 --> 00:14:52.236
The dinner party was planned for tonight,
right? That's why you're...!

00:14:52.674 --> 00:14:55.905
Yes, but Lady Shurei's house
is in that direction.

00:14:57.145 --> 00:15:00.410
I-I like to take the long route.
Anything wrong with that?!

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:07.217
Welcome. Please come in.

00:15:09.624 --> 00:15:12.252
The house and courtyard
are the same as before.

00:15:12.627 --> 00:15:16.620
That's because all of the money
Advisor Sho gave me has been spent.

00:15:17.198 --> 00:15:19.166
All five hundred coins?

00:15:19.534 --> 00:15:21.331
I heard it was used
on things like...

00:15:21.402 --> 00:15:24.166
...repairing the temple school
and donations to the local doctors.

00:15:28.843 --> 00:15:32.711
Wow. Working directly under the king
at such a young age is really amazing.

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:34.805
The current king,
what kind of person is he?

00:15:34.882 --> 00:15:38.613
He's a childish,
natural airhead of a nineteen year old.

00:15:39.654 --> 00:15:41.918
That's right.
He is a natural airhead, isn't he?

00:15:41.990 --> 00:15:43.924
You know him too, Princess?

00:15:43.992 --> 00:15:45.357
K-Kind of.

00:15:45.760 --> 00:15:48.888
But even so, he may yet surprise us and
become someone of great significance.

00:15:48.963 --> 00:15:51.431
He has potential at the very least.

00:15:52.100 --> 00:15:53.431
Oh?

00:15:53.801 --> 00:15:57.430
By the way, Ensei,
I heard you're from Sa Province.

00:15:58.239 --> 00:16:00.002
How was it on the way here?

00:16:00.475 --> 00:16:02.102
"How was it", you ask.

00:16:02.176 --> 00:16:04.371
You must mean with regard
to the mountain bandits, right?

00:16:04.445 --> 00:16:06.379
They're very active.

00:16:08.082 --> 00:16:09.481
What are you talking about?

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:13.384
There have been reports of an influx
of bandits from Sa Province lately.

00:16:13.788 --> 00:16:15.915
The Urin Army is
also sending officers...

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:18.754
...to help guard the city and
capture the bandits.

00:16:18.826 --> 00:16:20.555
And with the situation
as it is...

00:16:20.628 --> 00:16:22.493
...I'd like to ask Seiran
to assist us as well.

00:16:23.097 --> 00:16:28.262
You're asking Seiran to catch bandits?!
But Seiran is only a granary guard!

00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:30.804
Advisor So and our field marshals
are insisting...

00:16:30.872 --> 00:16:33.204
...and won't take no for an answer.

00:16:33.307 --> 00:16:36.174
They're all impressed
by Seiran's skills.

00:16:37.879 --> 00:16:38.846
But still...!

00:16:39.013 --> 00:16:44.212
It's only a temporary job, so he'll be able
to return to his old position in no time.

00:16:44.819 --> 00:16:45.945
Well, possibly.

00:16:48.222 --> 00:16:50.918
General Ran.
How about this man?

00:16:51.659 --> 00:16:55.459
He has good skills, limitless energy,
and is cheap to employ.

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:58.328
Ah, wait a moment.
I have business to attend to.

00:16:58.399 --> 00:17:03.632
Well, if Seiran says so,
Ensei's skills must be beyond question.

00:17:03.705 --> 00:17:04.797
Absolutely.

00:17:04.872 --> 00:17:07.864
So he really is a trusted
and reliable friend.

00:17:10.912 --> 00:17:13.346
But even if he does end up
helping us...

00:17:13.414 --> 00:17:15.644
...I still won't give up
trying to persuade you.

00:17:17.885 --> 00:17:20.217
Is that so? I understand.

00:17:20.822 --> 00:17:22.050
Seiran.

00:17:22.623 --> 00:17:23.991
It'll be fine.

00:17:23.991 --> 00:17:26.391
I'll try to come back home
before dinner.

00:17:26.928 --> 00:17:28.896
I'll cut corners wherever I can...

00:17:28.963 --> 00:17:30.055
...and if there's danger...

00:17:30.131 --> 00:17:32.725
...I'll shield myself with the people
around me and run away.

00:17:33.668 --> 00:17:36.034
Ensei will take over in my place.

00:17:37.171 --> 00:17:39.731
Any problem with that,
freeloader?

00:17:39.807 --> 00:17:40.899
No.

00:17:41.142 --> 00:17:43.372
You'd better work hard
to help Lady Shurei.

00:17:43.444 --> 00:17:45.912
If anything happens,
I'll cut off that head of yours.

00:17:46.781 --> 00:17:48.248
Okay, okay.

00:17:49.083 --> 00:17:51.051
Are you that worried
about Seiran?

00:17:51.452 --> 00:17:54.012
No... It's just
that it's summer, and...!

00:17:54.088 --> 00:17:55.180
Summer?

00:17:56.324 --> 00:17:58.087
I-It's nothing, really.

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:07.868
Koyu, would you like
another helping?

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:12.340
Ah, all right.
Please give me a little more.

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:15.036
- And I'd also like to ask a favor of you.
- What is it?

00:18:15.109 --> 00:18:17.009
Do you want me
to catch bandits too?

00:18:17.078 --> 00:18:19.706
How would you like to work
in the Imperial Court for a month?

00:18:31.692 --> 00:18:33.990
You look troubled, young man.

00:18:35.463 --> 00:18:36.760
Advisor Sho.

00:18:39.133 --> 00:18:44.571
Oh, is this about allowing women to
take the National Exams? Interesting.

00:18:45.139 --> 00:18:49.803
If this proposal didn't carry such an
impure motive, I'd offer you my praise.

00:18:50.378 --> 00:18:52.141
You old bastard.

00:18:52.346 --> 00:18:55.247
You seem to have been
working very hard lately.

00:18:56.017 --> 00:19:00.750
You're not trying to have this passed
in time for the next sitting, are you?

00:19:01.389 --> 00:19:02.617
It's for Shurei.

00:19:03.791 --> 00:19:06.589
Shurei worked hard
for my sake...

00:19:06.661 --> 00:19:09.653
...so now it's my turn
to work hard for hers.

00:19:13.334 --> 00:19:14.358
What's that?

00:19:15.603 --> 00:19:17.503
Y-You mean this?

00:19:17.939 --> 00:19:22.535
A famous delicacy from an island
in the east. Dried pickled plums.

00:19:23.477 --> 00:19:24.671
Dried pickled plums?

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:30.016
Even if you want them I won't give them
to you. They're very hard to get, after all.

00:19:33.754 --> 00:19:35.984
The senior secretary's
personal assistant?!

00:19:36.424 --> 00:19:39.985
Even if they're short staffed, allowing me
to do an important job like that...!

00:19:40.061 --> 00:19:43.053
You'll only be running errands.
It's not really an important job.

00:19:44.966 --> 00:19:46.524
You're not interested?

00:19:46.767 --> 00:19:49.565
You don't wanna go back to the
Court where that stupid king is?

00:19:49.637 --> 00:19:52.936
It's not like that.
I quite enjoyed my stay there.

00:19:53.441 --> 00:19:58.208
And as General Ran was saying,
he has the potential to become great.

00:20:00.715 --> 00:20:02.945
But, if I go back there...

00:20:03.017 --> 00:20:05.247
...that dream that can never come true
will be rekindled.

00:20:05.319 --> 00:20:06.786
What a good opportunity.

00:20:07.321 --> 00:20:10.290
It's pretty rare to get a chance
to work in the Imperial Court.

00:20:10.491 --> 00:20:13.221
I'm not sure why
you're hesitating, Princess.

00:20:13.294 --> 00:20:16.058
In life, it's better to regret
something you've done...

00:20:16.130 --> 00:20:18.564
...rather than regret not
doing something, don't you think?

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:20.262
Ensei.

00:20:20.334 --> 00:20:23.929
Although I hate to admit it,
he has a point, Lady Shurei.

00:20:24.238 --> 00:20:26.866
If you want to do it, Shurei,
I don't have a problem with it.

00:20:27.074 --> 00:20:28.405
Seiran.

00:20:28.743 --> 00:20:29.971
Father.

00:20:36.450 --> 00:20:37.940
I gratefully accept.

00:20:39.153 --> 00:20:41.883
However, women aren't permitted
to work in the Outer Court...

00:20:41.956 --> 00:20:45.551
...so you'll have to dress in men's attire.
- W-Won't I be discovered?!

00:20:45.626 --> 00:20:47.389
There's no need to worry.

00:20:47.461 --> 00:20:50.862
With that figure of yours, there's no way
anyone will notice you're a woman.

00:20:59.106 --> 00:21:03.042
The senior secretary is bound to notice
that Shurei is a girl, isn't he?

00:21:04.045 --> 00:21:06.013
You may be right.

00:21:06.781 --> 00:21:09.477
But I have confidence in her.

00:21:14.121 --> 00:21:17.420
The future the king is working towards
is really something to look forward to.

00:21:17.491 --> 00:21:19.186
Isn't it, Enjun?

00:21:32.673 --> 00:21:34.971
- It really suits you.
- Yes.

00:21:35.042 --> 00:21:37.169
No one would take you
for a girl.

00:21:37.244 --> 00:21:39.303
You really make a great boy.

00:21:40.281 --> 00:21:42.909
Is this supposed to make me
happy or sad?

00:21:43.551 --> 00:21:45.246
Well then, I'll be going.

00:21:45.619 --> 00:21:47.052
Take care.

00:21:49.390 --> 00:21:50.414
Hey!

00:21:51.559 --> 00:21:54.528
- You're going too.
- Huh? Me too?

00:21:54.595 --> 00:21:58.895
Of course. Stay by her side.
If anything should happen...!

00:21:58.966 --> 00:22:03.027
You'll cut off this head of mine, right?
I get it, I get it, all right!

00:22:03.771 --> 00:22:06.296
Hey, wait up, Princess!

00:22:16.150 --> 00:22:18.175
I never thought I would
come here again.

00:22:23.057 --> 00:22:25.389
What is the senior secretary like?

00:22:25.860 --> 00:22:28.488
He's very capable, touted to be
the next prime minister...

00:22:28.562 --> 00:22:30.621
...but he's a strange,
mysterious man.

00:22:31.365 --> 00:22:34.425
He's of the Kou Family.
His name is Kijin Kou.

00:22:34.502 --> 00:22:39.030
What? Um, don't tell me
that's "Kijin" as in "weirdo".

00:22:40.241 --> 00:22:43.506
That's right. However,
I understand his real name is different.

00:22:44.478 --> 00:22:47.140
With people around him always
calling him Kijin, meaning weirdo...

00:22:47.214 --> 00:22:49.011
...he decided to change his name.

00:22:49.717 --> 00:22:52.709
So even in the Royal Court there are
interesting characters like that, I guess.

00:22:53.087 --> 00:22:54.782
By the way, Secretary Ri...

00:22:55.189 --> 00:22:57.657
...you said we'd be at the Ministry of
Finance within thirty minutes...

00:22:57.725 --> 00:23:00.523
...but it's been almost two hours.
Aren't we there yet?

00:23:03.864 --> 00:23:06.025
Just when did the Ministry
of Finance move?!

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:07.692
So we're lost.

00:23:10.071 --> 00:23:13.234
Shu Hong and Ensei Ro
have arrived.

00:23:14.708 --> 00:23:17.734
This is the Senior Secretary
of the Ministry of Finance, Kijin Kou.

00:23:18.779 --> 00:23:20.269
This guy definitely is...

00:23:20.347 --> 00:23:21.644
...a weirdo.

00:23:30.558 --> 00:23:35.655
Itsumo sugoku jiyu na anata ha ima

00:23:35.863 --> 00:23:42.200
Kono ame no naka donna
Yume wo oikaketeiruno

00:23:42.503 --> 00:23:47.463
Dokokade kodoku to tatakainagara

00:23:47.675 --> 00:23:52.772
Namida mo gaman shiterundarou

00:23:53.781 --> 00:23:58.184
Hitori demo daijobu to

00:23:59.720 --> 00:24:04.851
Anata mo watashi to onaji

00:24:05.626 --> 00:24:16.195
Tomawari bakari dakedo
Nazeka kono michi ga suki de

00:24:17.071 --> 00:24:22.668
Shiawase da toka ureshii toki ha

00:24:23.077 --> 00:24:28.140
Anata no koto wo omoidasu kara

00:24:29.016 --> 00:24:34.579
Iroazayaka na kisetsu ha kitto

00:24:34.955 --> 00:24:41.758
Kono omoi todoketekureru

00:24:45.065 --> 00:24:45.566
Next Episode

00:24:45.566 --> 00:24:47.601
Next Episode
I've come to the palace again...

00:24:47.601 --> 00:24:47.635
Next Episode

00:24:47.635 --> 00:24:48.169
Next Episode
...and met a strange person.

00:24:48.169 --> 00:24:49.803
Next Episode
A Journey of a Thousand
Miles Begins with a Single Step
...and met a strange person.

00:24:49.803 --> 00:24:49.837
Next Episode
A Journey of a Thousand
Miles Begins with a Single Step

00:24:49.837 --> 00:24:52.173
Next Episode
A Journey of a Thousand
Miles Begins with a Single Step
Although I've met quite a few
strange people...

00:24:52.173 --> 00:24:52.206
Next Episode
A Journey of a Thousand
Miles Begins with a Single Step

00:24:52.206 --> 00:24:54.375
Next Episode
A Journey of a Thousand
Miles Begins with a Single Step
...this is the first time I've met
a man wearing a mask.

00:24:54.375 --> 00:24:54.841
...this is the first time I've met
a man wearing a mask.

00:24:55.209 --> 00:24:57.336
Kijin Kou. A mysterious man.
